From: Doruk Aktun <info@dorukaktun.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: Don't enable parents when reparenting orphans

clk_core_reparent_orphans_nolock() uses __clk_set_parent_before() and
__clk_set_parent_after() to migrate the prepare/enable count of an
orphan. For a CLK_OPS_PARENT_ENABLE orphan these also prepare and
enable the new parent around the reparent, but no clk_ops is called on
the orphan here, so there is nothing that needs the parent running.

It also goes wrong when the new parent cannot be enabled yet. On SM8350
the DSI PHY registers its PLL outputs and the display clock controller's
pixel clock sources (CLK_OPS_PARENT_ENABLE) are reparented to them in
of_clk_add_hw_provider(). The PLL has no rate yet and fails to lock, the
error of clk_core_prepare_enable() is ignored, and
__clk_set_parent_after() then disables and unprepares a parent that was
never enabled:

  DSI PLL(0) lock failed, status=0x00000000
  dsi0_phy_pll_out_dsiclk already disabled
  WARNING: drivers/clk/clk.c:1257 at clk_core_disable+0x288/0x2c0
  dsi0_phy_pll_out_dsiclk already unprepared
  WARNING: drivers/clk/clk.c:1116 at clk_core_unprepare+0x2e8/0x320

Only migrate the prepare/enable count when reparenting orphans.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
diff --git a/drivers/clk/clk.c b/drivers/clk/clk.c
index fef87167a..e54b71aba 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/clk.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/clk.c
@@ -3935,15 +3935,36 @@ static void clk_core_reparent_orphans_nolock(void)
 		struct clk_core *parent = __clk_init_parent(orphan);
 
 		/*
-		 * We need to use __clk_set_parent_before() and _after() to
-		 * properly migrate any prepare/enable count of the orphan
-		 * clock. This is important for CLK_IS_CRITICAL clocks, which
-		 * are enabled during init but might not have a parent yet.
+		 * Migrate any prepare/enable count of the orphan clock to its
+		 * new parent. This is important for CLK_IS_CRITICAL clocks,
+		 * which are enabled during init but might not have a parent
+		 * yet.
+		 *
+		 * This only updates the topology, no clk_ops is called on the
+		 * orphan, so CLK_OPS_PARENT_ENABLE does not apply here. Doing
+		 * the parent enable dance of __clk_set_parent_before() anyway
+		 * is not only useless: if the new parent cannot be enabled yet
+		 * (e.g. an unconfigured PLL that fails to lock), the failure is
+		 * ignored and __clk_set_parent_after() then disables and
+		 * unprepares a parent that was never enabled, triggering the
+		 * "already disabled" and "already unprepared" warnings.
 		 */
 		if (parent) {
+			unsigned long flags;
+
+			if (orphan->prepare_count) {
+				clk_core_prepare_enable(parent);
+				clk_core_enable_lock(orphan);
+			}
+
 			/* update the clk tree topology */
-			__clk_set_parent_before(orphan, parent);
-			__clk_set_parent_after(orphan, parent, NULL);
+			flags = clk_enable_lock();
+			clk_reparent(orphan, parent);
+			clk_enable_unlock(flags);
+
+			if (orphan->prepare_count)
+				clk_core_disable_lock(orphan);
+
 			__clk_recalc_accuracies(orphan);
 			__clk_recalc_rates(orphan, true, 0);
 
